draft.methodology:
I combined four independent research lenses (press, primary documents, headcount, recent). They overlapped heavily and agreed on every reported number. PnL is IMC's own 'net trading revenues' line. For FY2020-2025 it comes from audited annual reports (2021, 2023, 2024 and 2025, including their prior-year comparatives). For 2015-2019 it comes from Quote/FD/Amsterdamtrader articles quoting the KvK-filed accounts. No 2018 figure was ever published, so I rebuilt it from reported net profit, cost per employee and the opex trend. 2026 is a run-rate estimate, because IMC publishes no interim results. EUR figures were converted at annual-average rates, except 2023, where IMC's own USD restatement was used. Headcount is an annual average:
- reported averages for 2015-2016 and 2022;
- averages of consecutive year-end figures for 2020-2025, cross-checked against the CO2-per-employee denominators in the annual reports;
- a cost-per-head model plus interpolation for 2017-2019.
Error bars are about 90% intervals scaled to source quality: ±1-2% for audited USD figures, ±2-4% for press-quoted accounts plus FX, about -15%/+18% for the rebuilt 2018 figure, and about -36%/+40% for 2026.
